    "explanation": {
      "text": "In the first audit the tool flagged a **proxy\u2011feature leak**: the column\u202f`account_closed_flag` alone gave an AUC of\u202f0.971, meaning the model could almost perfectly predict the target from that single field. Because the feature directly mirrors the outcome, it makes cross\u2011validation scores look unrealistically high even though the model would not generalize to new data. We fixed this by **dropping the leaking column** and reran the checks (round\u202f2), after which the best single\u2011feature AUC fell to\u202f0.662 and all other leakage metrics stayed at\u202f0.0. The final evaluation will use stratified CV without `account_closed_flag`, with no rows removed, and the leakage issue is now resolved.",
